{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"c1fb6ba6e10cf32408b2b10111707435607464f831f5e00e125267521e61a833","digest":{"component_or_area":"test_event_append_index_lock","key_entities":["tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_index_lock.py::test_contended_index_lock_cleared_during_backoff_succeeds","src/rebar/_store/event_append.py","gitutil._with_index_lock_retry","gitutil._retry_probe","_reclaim_if_stale_index_lock","stage_and_commit","_git_add","_git_commit","index.lock","_is_git_lock_error"],"problem_keywords":["flaky test","test-timing","index lock","macOS","py3.13","git commit","race condition"],"propositions":["Test plants a young index.lock and uses threading.Timer to delete it, but timer can fire while git commit owns its own real index.lock, causing fatal write failure on slow runners","Test's timer-based lock deletion has no identity check, so it cannot distinguish between planted lock and git's legitimate lock","On slow macOS py3.13 CI runner, git commit still holds lock at timer fire time (t=0.4s), resulting in StoreError: unable to write new index file","Production code path is correct and succeeds; failure is caused entirely by test's own timer deleting a lock owned by code under test","gitutil._retry_probe seam provides deterministic alternative to timer-based lock release for test, firing after each retry attempt instead of wall-clock time"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787673658181105001,"uuid":"99a2ecac-44e0-45ba-b1da-2159e0101d32"}